# The projection editor's arrangement rows (Scenograph editor plan, E5): one
# row per declared option, placeholders that say what a blank row means, a
# refusal in the compiler's words, and rows rebuilt when the arrangement
# changes. The practice projection starts on Grid with three items.
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
act load-practice-projection
settle 2
click role:tab Arrangement
settle 2
assert retained {"role":"textbox","label":"Cell width","attribute":"placeholder","value":"164 (the largest item's width)"}
assert retained {"role":"textbox","label":"Columns","attribute":"placeholder","value":"2 (the side of the square that holds every item)"}
click role:textbox Columns
input-text 0
settle 2
assert retained {"role":"status","label":"Columns refusal","text":"needs a positive whole number"}
assert retained {"role":"textbox","label":"Columns","attribute":"aria-invalid","value":"true"}
assert snap projection-executable == false
click role:textbox Columns
input-text 3
settle 2
assert retained {"role":"textbox","label":"Columns","attribute":"aria-invalid","value":"false"}
assert snap projection-executable == true
click role:textbox Arrangement kind
input-text spiral
settle 2
assert retained {"role":"group","label":"Arrangement options","text":"Curve"}
click role:combobox Curve
settle 1
click role:option linear
settle 1
settle 2
assert snap projection-executable == true
click role:textbox Arrangement kind
input-text nothing.like.it
settle 2
assert retained {"role":"group","label":"Arrangement options","text":"names no built-in arrangement or registered solver"}
capture projection_options
wait
log projection editor arrangement rows proof complete
